  "sourcePolicy": "Live means regularly updated third-party model output, not observation at the breaking wave. Experimental spot-fit scores remain uncalibrated. Official marine/weather alerts from DMC, Armada and SENAPRED require manual verification until a dependable licensed API is implemented. API timestamps are requested as Unix UTC instants and rendered with the IANA spot timezone, not the provider's response-wide fixed UTC offset. Secondary and tertiary partitions are optional and never imputed. Ventanas is a fifth modelled research-only break with a separately maintained access restriction; no surfing recommendation or ranking while reported restriction remains unverified lifted. Open-Meteo sea_level_height_msl at coarse ~8-km tide/ocean model resolution is displayed as sea-level context ONLY, never scored as a local tide optimum or navigation estimate. Optional partition coverage requires both model hours.",
